    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31208" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἱρμός</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴρω</span> A) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>train, series, sequence</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				916a31
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				3.1.2
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἱ. αἰτιῶν</span>
			<i>concatenation</i> of causes, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Placit.</u>
				1.28.4
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				1.5.17
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἱρμός</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.284
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hierocl.
				<u>in CA</u>
				11p.442M.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>connexion</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἱ. λόγου πρὸς βίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.569
				</span></i>
			.</div>
